Well, Muppet IV died in the Arena. I would not call it a STUPID death,
exactly, but he did make several tactical mistakes which probably cost
his life. Although entering the Arena with AC 3 and no healing other
than ring of regeneration is probably not advisable either.

Several times Muppet went down the stairs, zapped or clobbered a few
monsters, then ran back up the stairs and waited for the ring to bring
him back up to full HP. At one point he went up the stairs with HP in
single digits. When fire giants sidled up to the staircase, Muppet woud
have only one turn before he had to go back up. Clearly this was going
nowhere. So next time he went down, first thing Muppet did was read a
scroll of earth.

Good idea in itself -- nearby monsters got conked on the head, and once
Muppet killed them, he had a nice fort for a breathing space. Then he
pick-axed one boulder to make a killing alley. Mistake #1: it was an
UNCURSED scroll. I should have blessed it first (and I could!). Once
Muppet moved off the staircase, his retreat was blocked.

Even so, Muppet managed kill the most dangerous enemies -- the leopard
and all but one fire giant (I think that one was asleep in the end), --
orcs, blobs and such were a small bother, and he just needed to tackle
to couatles. Victory seemed possible, but... mistake #2: do not leave
scrolls of create monster lying around!

Muppet actually walked over the scroll and did not bother to pick it
up. Well, a couatl picked it up, read it, and suddenly things got a lot
worse. Perhaps picking that scroll still would not have saved Muppet
because just before he died, a couatl read ANOTHER create monster
scroll. OTOH, he'd have a chance if he avoided mistake #2 AND mistake
#3: not reading his one remaining scroll of teleportation.

I just plain forgot about that scroll. Granted, with couatls having
pretty much re-populated the Arena, that scroll would have done little
good, but still it was a mistake.

Three tactical errors, any ONE of them probably not lethal, but
together... a learning experience.


